# SABOTAGE: PP-13 (tenant reveal-approver surface) — drops the `org_filter(org_id)` conjunct
# from `Samen.Approvals.list_pending/3` (the org-scoped pending read the approver surface
# consults via `Samen.Reveal.Grants.pending_for_org/2`), replacing it with a no-op passthrough
# that still references `org_id` (so it compiles) but no longer scopes the query. Without the
# filter, `pending_for_org(org_b)` returns org_A's pending `pii_reveal` approvals — a
# tenant approver in one org could see (and act on) another org's pending reveal requests.
# The `drop-the-org-filter-must-flip-a-named-test` org-scope pin.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/reveal_approver_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a different org sees NONE of another org
# APPLY: git apply scripts/sabotages/188-pp13-reveal-approver-org-scope-drop.patch
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/approvals.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/approvals.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/approvals.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/approvals.ex
@@ -165,7 +165,7 @@ defmodule Samen.Approvals do
       query =
         res
         |> Ash.Query.filter(state == :pending and kind == ^kind)
-        |> org_filter(org_id)
+        |> tap(fn _ -> org_id end)
         |> Ash.Query.sort(requested_at: :asc)
 
       # authz-scope: org-pinned one clause down via org_filter/2 (binary org => org_id == ^org_id;
